From afb69e0ce6fe2e7a0985af25d85abee643d0c801 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xenlib: DomD-as-toolstack xenstore support

DomD-as-toolstack: let an external privileged control domain (DomD, a
dom0less domain with capabilities=0x1) create/destroy guests via `xl create`/
`xl destroy` against the thin Zephyr Dom0 xenstore server. Verified on RPi5:
DomD `xl create` completes (rc=0) and the guest reaches RUNNING (with a
DomD-side console seeder that satisfies libxl's console waits).

  * xen-dom-mgmt.c/.h: xs_introduce_domain() / xs_release_domain() — register/
    release a toolstack-created guest in xenstore (shadow xen_domain, ring map,
    evtchn bind, xs_initialize_xenstore, domain_list). domid0 reject, DOMU_MAX
    guard, refcount-respecting release (no hypervisor destroy — DomD owns it).
  * xenstore_srv.c: handle_introduce (XS_INTRODUCE op8) / handle_release
    (XS_RELEASE op9) + table entries + wire NUL-bound parse + is_privileged +
    ESRCH->ENOENT; notify_watchers("@introduceDomain"/"@releaseDomain");
    transaction handling made non-blocking (running_transaction as a count) so
    DomD's multiplexed xl+xenconsoled transactions no longer collide.

Depends on 0005 (xenlib initrd) and 0006 (xenstore toolstack-domid).
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-4-8
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
